  "rationale": "Yusa human knockout library (about 90,700 guides, 5 per gene, no non-targeting controls) in BETi-sensitive parental OCI-AML2 cells and in JQ1-resistant OCI-AML2 cells (Romine et al. 2021). GEO's overall design: compare sgRNA counts between DMSO and BETi at matching time points. Each day-14 library was sequenced twice (_addtl); the re-reads agree near-Poisson and are summed by prepare.R. Analysis 1, parental cells JQ1 vs DMSO at day 14: knockouts that confer resistance are enriched (the abstract names SPI1, JUNB, FOS, AHR and ARNT as determinants of response). Analysis 2, JQ1-resistant cells JQ1 vs DMSO at day 14: knockouts that restore sensitivity are depleted (BCL2, CDK6). JQ1 and DMSO arms are separate cultures, so no pairing term. The day-21 CPI-0610 arm is kept in counts.tsv but not analyzed.",
